## 2. Colour: primitives → semantics → CSS variables

### 2.1 Source files

| Layer | Where to look |
|--------|----------------|
| Design token definitions | `configs/design-tokens.json` → `color-primitives`, `color-semantics` |
| Runtime (auto light/dark) | Generated `src/commonStyles/sass-generated/variables.css` → `--background-*`, `--text-*`, `--icon-*`, `--border-*`, `--surface-*`, `--overlay-*`, component-specific vars |
| Storybook catalogue | Story **PODS Colors/Colors** (`src/stories-common/Color/`) + `Colors.mdx` (lists variable names and usage patterns) |
| Figma link | In `Colors.mdx` / `Number.mdx` (Design Tokens file) |

### 2.2 Primitive families (JSON paths)

Use these buckets when reasoning about “which primitive backs a semantic”:

- `color-primitives.sky-blue.*` — primary / link family
- `color-primitives.mono.*` — neutrals, surfaces, text greys
- `color-primitives.pearl.*`, `color-primitives.sky-blue.*` (offset rows) — offset backgrounds
- `color-primitives.red.*`, `color-primitives.orange.*`, `color-primitives.green.*` — negative / notice / positive
- `color-primitives.shadow.*` — alpha-stacked shadow tints on `#101010`
- Additional semantic-only rows in CSS: `--pastel-01-strong` … `--pastel-12-weak`, badge/chips/switch helpers (see `variables.css`)

### 2.3 Semantic roles → CSS variables (naming pattern)

**Do not hand-pick greys.** Map UI roles to variables:

| Role | Typical variables (see `variables.css` for full set) |
|------|--------------------------------------------------------|
| Page / card surfaces | `--surface-level-1` … `--surface-level-4`, `--background-neutral-inverse` |
| Primary actions & links | `--text-primary-medium`, `--text-primary-strong`, `--background-primary-medium`, `--border-primary-medium` |
| Body text | `--text-neutral-strong`, `--text-neutral-moderate`, `--text-neutral-medium`, `--text-neutral-weak` |
| Status | `--text-negative-strong`, `--text-notice-strong`, `--text-positive-strong` (+ matching `--background-*`, `--icon-*`, `--border-*`) |
| Overlays | `--overlay-strong`, `--overlay-weak` |
| Brand (non-semantic UI) | `--brand-primary`, `--brand-secondary` |
| Secondary body / helper lines (readability) | `--text-neutral-moderate` |
| Tertiary / placeholder / de-emphasised UI copy | `--text-neutral-medium` |

**Dark mode:** the same variable *names* swap values under `@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark)` in `variables.css`.

