## 3. Typography rules

### 3.1 Font stack

Applied globally in `src/commonStyles/sass-generated/index.css` (and source `_modified-normalize.scss`): **`inter-subset`** with system UI fallbacks. Weights 400 / 500 / 600 / 700 are loaded per face.

### 3.2 Scale & weights (token IDs)

**Canonical data:** `configs/design-tokens.json` → `typography.scale`, `typography.weight`.

**Scale keys** (as shown in Storybook; display names may be overridden in `src/stories-common/Typography/styleConfigs.ts`):

- Display: `display1`, `display2`, `display3` (and any additional keys present in JSON)
- Titles: `title1` … `title4`
- Body: `body`, `subtext`, `caption`
- Story-only labels: `tab-bar`, `overline1`, `overline2` (when present in token data / style config)

**Weight keys:** `regular` (400), `medium` (500), `semibold` (600), `bold` (700).

Each scale entry exposes `font-size`, `line-height`, and `letter-spacing` objects with a `value` field — Storybook **PODS Typography/Typography** renders the matrix from this JSON.

### 3.3 Using type in code

- **SCSS mixins:** Storybook typography pages use helpers like `getFontStyle(title3-bold, …)` (see `Typography.module.scss`) — follow the same mixin pattern as other pods-components.
- **Colour on type:** pair scale with semantic text colours, e.g. `var(--text-neutral-strong)` for primary reading text.

### 3.4 Landing title in **Header Default** (large / extended row)

- **Do not** add a **SectionHeader** for the same primary screen title when that title already appears on **`HeaderDefault`** **`size="large"`** second row — one hierarchy owner for the H1-level label.
- The main title string on that second row uses **`typography.scale.display3`** + **`typography.weight.bold`** and **`var(--text-neutral-strong)`** (implementation: `getFontStyle(display3-bold, …)`). The optional line below stays **`body`** + **`medium`** + **`var(--text-neutral-moderate)`** unless a component story specifies otherwise.
- **Figma reference:** “Design Standardisation for Gen AI” — Header component node `118:4466` in file `e58GKvGTgkVs6jputDoINS`.
- **Do not** pull in Material / M3 static type tokens for PODS screens — stay on `typography.scale` / `typography.weight` from `design-tokens.json`.

