### 5.3 `HeaderDefault` — trailing icons (`TrailingIcons`)

`HeaderTrailing` (`pods-components/Header/HeaderTrailing.tsx`) wraps **each** `TrailingIcons` entry in a `<span>` that uses **`Header.module.scss`** `.icon`: a **24×24px** slot, with **`& > *`** sizing the **immediate child** to the same touch/icon size.

- **Do** pass **unwrapped** icon nodes as `TrailingIcons` elements — typically the SVG **`ReactComponent`** from `@paytm-h5-common/.../ultra-icons/...`, with **`role="button"`**, **`tabIndex={0}`**, **`aria-label`**, **`onClick`**, and **`onKeyDown`** (activate on Enter/Space) on **that icon element**. Optional: **`style={{ cursor: "pointer" }}`** when not using a filled hit target.
- **Don’t** wrap those icons in **extra** story/layout `<span>`s (or other containers) that apply smaller **`svg { width/height }`** rules or arbitrary sizes. An extra wrapper becomes the `.icon > *` target, so the **inner** SVG may no longer receive the header’s 24×24 rule and can render **too small** or inconsistently — especially with **two** trailing icons (`MAX_TRAILING_ITEMS` = 2 in `Header.types.ts`).
- **Don’t** rely on deprecated story-only header icon wrappers; keep parity with **`PODS Components/Header/Header Default`** behaviour.

**Consumption:** `import { Button, … } from '@paytm-h5-common/paytm_common_ui'` (see Introduction story).

**Per-component rules:** each story file documents props via Storybook Docs (`autodocs: true` in `.storybook/main.js`). Prefer **controls + ArgsTable** over duplicating measurements in markdown.

### 5.3a **`Button`** **`type="filled"`** — label vs icon colour

**Implementation:** **`pods-components/Button/Button.module.scss`**.

- **Label** on **`filled`**: **`--text-universal-light`** (inverse primary copy).
- **Leading / trailing SVGs** (selectors **`.leadingIcon svg`**, **`.trailingIcon svg`**): **`--icon-universal-light`** — icon semantic for glyphs on the primary fill, not **`--text-universal-light`** (aligns with **FAB**, **Badge**, and other inverse primary chrome).
- **Disabled** **`filled`**: label **`--text-neutral-medium`**, SVGs **`--icon-neutral-medium`**.
- **Consumers:** do not put **`color`** / **`fill`** **inline** on SVG nodes passed as **`LeadingIcon`** / **`TrailingIcon`** unless you intend to override the component; inline rules outrank the module and break token tinting. Prefer **ultra-icons** paths that use **`currentColor`**. Do not add screen CSS that shrinks **leading** / **trailing** SVGs in ways that fight **`Button`**’s size tokens (**`large`** → **24×24** icon slot, etc.).

### 5.4 **`ListItem` leading **`Avatar`** (logo / profile) — no skewed rasters

**`PODS Components/List`** **`ListItem`** with **`leading={{ type: "avatar", … }}`** renders **`PODS Components/Avatar`** (same sources as **`paytm_common_ui`** / Storybook **`pods-components`**; production **`import … from '@paytm-h5-common/paytm_common_ui'`**).

- **Circular raster treatment:** **`Avatar`** **`type="logo"`** (**`logo-image`**) and **`type="profile"`** must fill the **token-sized** circle (**`small`**, **`regular`**, **`large`**, …) **without** non-uniform scaling. The library uses **`width: 100%`**, **`height: 100%`**, **`object-fit: cover`**, **`object-position: center`**, **`display: block`**, and **`overflow: hidden`** on the **avatar container** so rectangular product/photo assets stay **proportionally** cropped inside the circle — not stretched or “skewed.”
- **Do not** override with **`customClass`** / screen SCSS that forces **`img`** to different **width** and **height** without **`object-fit`**, or that sets **`flex-grow: 1`** / **`height: 100%`** on **`leading-avatar`** / **`avatar-logo-container`** wrappers — that **breaks** aspect ratio. If you need a **letterboxed** brand mark (full logo visible, not cropped), treat it as a **product** choice and use **`object-fit: contain`** **only** via an approved **Avatar** / design-system update, not one-off list CSS.
- **`ListItem`** **`leadingSection`** may **`align-self: stretch`** to the row height; the **Avatar** chip itself remains fixed to the **`size`** token — do not stretch the **Avatar** root to the full row height in consumer layouts.

### 5.5 **Bill / saved-account hub** (Card + `ListItem` + promo strip + FAB)

Use for screens that list **saved payees** (electricity, water, BBPS-style hubs). **Reference:** **`docs/layout-references/layouts.md`** (bill-pay hub flows) and **PODS Components** (**Card**, **List**, **FAB**).

| Topic | Rule |
|--------|------|
| **Row surface** | One **`Card`** per row; **`List`** with a **single** **`ListItem`** per card (`separator={false}`). Page wash **`--surface-level-4`** (or shell equivalent); card fill **`--surface-level-1`**. |
| **Card elevation** | **Do not** add **`box-shadow`** or other discretionary elevation on these **Card**s unless the product spec or design explicitly requests it. Use surface contrast + radius; **`border: none`** on tiles-on-wash is OK for hub-style bill rows—**without** stacking shadow. |
| **Horizontal offer / promo strip** | When the design is **one row**: leading mark (e.g. circular icon) + primary copy + **`Button`** **`type="link"`** (e.g. “View All ›”) on the right, **prefer a token-composed strip** over **`Alerts`** if **`Alerts`** layout does not match (stacking, typography, or action placement). Build with **`--background-positive-weak`**, **`--text-positive-strong`**, **`--icon-positive-strong`**, **`Button`** link, plus **`$radius-*`**, **`$padding-*`**, **`$gap-*`**. Use **`PODS Components/Alerts`** when the real pattern matches its **block** / **inline** stories. |
| **Leading `Avatar` (multi-line rows)** | **`type="logo"`** with **biller** marks per row (§5.4); **`leading.size: "regular"`**, **`leading.position: "top"`**. Production passes **`billerLogoImage`** / **`billerLogoAlt`**. |
| **Trailing overflow** | **`trailing.type: "icon"`** with **`position: "top"`** for vertical ellipsis / overflow; **`stopPropagation`** on icon **`onClick`** / keyboard activation so row **`onClick`** does not fire. |
| **Primary add action** | **`FAB`** for **Add …** when it is the screen’s main action; position inside the same framed shell as other product screens (override fixed positioning if the story uses a phone preview). |

