## 6. Layout & elevation principles

- **Default canvas:** global `body` background uses `var(--surface-level-1)` (`index.css`).
- **Cards & sheets:** rely on component implementations in Storybook (e.g. **BottomSheet**, **Card**) — they consume semantic colours and number tokens internally. **PODS Card** default inner padding is **16px** on all sides (`number-semantics.padding.horizontal-3xl` / `vertical-3xl`, `number-primitives.unit-6`).
- **List-hub Cards and shadow:** do not add discretionary **`box-shadow`** on **Card** tiles in saved-account / bill-hub lists unless asked—see **§5.5**.
- **Elevation / scrim:** use `--overlay-strong` / `--overlay-weak` for modal scrims; shadow stacks should trace back to `color-primitives.shadow.*` where components use tokenised shadows.
- **Screen layout inventory (product flows):** `docs/layout-references/layouts.md` — Figma-derived **structure, flow, per-screen ASCII region sketch**, and suggested Paytm common UI composition (semantic only; no pixel or hex in prose or diagrams). Patterns are **cross-vertical**: any team may reuse an entry when the **use case** matches (same screen job / structure), not only the vertical named in the file title. When building or extending screens, use this file for **which blocks and patterns** apply; use §2–§5 here for **tokens and components**. Regenerate or edit that doc when flows change (see **`prompts/hi-pods.md`** **MODE B** at repo root); do not mirror its full content inside `.cursor`.
- **Reusable layout pattern menu:** `docs/layout-references/layout-pattern-catalog.md` — **50 generic shells** (`LP-01` … `LP-50`) with use-when cues, Paytm component families, and compact ASCII. **When implementing a new screen:** (1) Check `layouts.md` for a concrete match; if none, (2) pick the closest **`LP-NN`** (or compose two, e.g. list body + sheet overlay), (3) state the chosen pattern ID in reasoning or PR text when helpful. Do not treat catalog entries as pixel specs — tokens and Storybook variants still win.

