## 8. Do’s and don’ts (token-first)

### Do

- Use **semantic CSS variables** (`--text-*`, `--background-*`, `--surface-*`, `--border-*`, `--icon-*`) for any new UI; let light/dark swap automatically.
- Use **number-semantics** (`margin`, `padding`, `gap`, `radius`) or their SCSS aliases instead of arbitrary `px` values.
- Use **typography.scale** + **typography.weight** from `design-tokens.json` for type sizing.
- Open the **matching Storybook story** when describing or implementing a component variant.

### Don’t

- **Don’t pierce or override `pods-components` internals from pattern / story / app SCSS** — no `:global([data-testid="…"])`, `:deep`, or descendant selectors that change **typography, colours, padding, or borders inside** shipped components (**Badge**, **Button**, **ListItem**, etc.). **Allowed:** layout wrappers around the component (`flex`, `gap`, `min-width`, **`customClass` only where the component documents it as a safe outer shell**). If the design needs a new size or density, add a **documented prop or variant in `pods-components`** (or a new token-backed component) instead of local overrides.
- Don’t embed one-off hex values in prompts or specs when a **semantic variable** or **primitive path** exists.
- Don’t bypass the token file: if a value is missing, extend **`design-tokens.json`** and regenerate styles rather than hardcoding in product code.
- Don’t describe type using **external systems** (e.g. Material static “body medium”) when **`typography.scale`** / **`typography.weight`** entries exist for the same role.
- **Don’t add extra `margin-top`, spacer divs, or section-level flex `gap` between `SectionHeader` and its immediately following `Card`.** Wrap **`SectionHeader` + `Card`** in one column with **`gap: 0`**. The **only** vertical space between the section label and the card top should be **`SectionHeader`’s own bottom padding** (**`padding-vertical-xl`** = **8px** per tokens) — not **`gap.4xl`**. See **§8.1a** and **§11**.
- Don’t use **`disabled`** on a **primary flow CTA** (e.g. **Proceed**, **Continue**, **Pay**) to communicate “form not ready.” Keep that button **enabled**; on tap, run validation and show problems with **TextField** **`error`** / assistive copy where the issue belongs, or with **Alerts** (**`layout="inline"`** in-flow, **`layout="block"`** for screen-level banners) when there is no single field owner. **Exception:** short **in-flight** guards (e.g. **`loading`** while a payment call runs) may still avoid double submission — prefer **`loading`** + idempotent handlers over greying out the main action for validation reasons.

### 8.1 Composition principles

These rules are intended to be **generally applicable PODS composition guidance**, not one-off harness shortcuts.

| Principle | Meaning |
|-----------|---------|
| **One horizontal inset owner** | In any region, only one layer owns the outer left/right gutter: page shell, **Card**, **BottomSheet**, inline surface, or row wrapper. Child roots may keep **interior** padding, but they should not re-apply page gutter. |
| **One vertical rhythm owner per boundary** | Space **between** sections, **within** a card, and **within** a control stack should come from the parent rhythm rule for that boundary. Do not stack parent `gap` with child `margin-block` unless the pattern explicitly calls for both. |
| **Surface owns comfort padding** | Components that paint a surface or control shell (for example **Card**, **Search**, **Alerts**, **SegmentedControl**, **BottomSheet**) usually keep their **interior** padding even when the page shell owns outer gutter. |
| **Rows inherit parent inset** | Repeating rows inside a parent surface (for example **ListItem**, custom settings rows, selectable rows) should inherit the parent inset when that parent already owns horizontal spacing. Strip duplicate row padding where needed, then re-stretch separators to the new span. |
| **Overlays belong to the layout that launches them** | Portaled UI should visually belong to the same frame/shell/surface that launches it. If the app is framed in a preview shell, attach overlays to that shell; if the app is truly full-bleed, attach to the app root. |
| **Section chrome stays outside elevated content by default** | Page-level **Header** and section-level **SectionHeader** label the content that follows; they should usually stay outside **Card** and precede it directly. |
| **Proximity beats generic gaps** | **Gestalt (grouping):** blocks that answer one user question or deliver one message (title + supporting lines, bullets that belong together, helper + legal line + text link) should sit **close** — use **small** token steps between them (`gap.m` … `gap.2xl`, or type line-height alone). Reserve **`gap.3xl`** and larger **only between separate ideas** (e.g. disclaimer cluster vs primary actions, or two unrelated sections). Reusing **section-sized** vertical rhythm **between every** text sibling turns one message into scattered islands and breaks layout **gestalt**. |

**Proximity → token mapping (quick rule of thumb):**
- **Within one cluster** (lines forming a single thought): `gap.m` (4px) to `gap.xl` (8px)
- **Between clusters in the same section/surface**: `gap.2xl` (12px) to `gap.3xl` (16px)
- **Between sections on the page**: `gap.4xl` (24px)
- **After hero header to first section**: `gap.xl` (8px)

### 8.1a Vertical rhythm quick reference

**Scan this table first** when deciding which gap token to use between two vertical neighbours. Detailed rationale lives in **§11**; this is the lookup.

| Transition (top → bottom) | Gap token | Value | Key rule |
|----------------------------|-----------|-------|----------|
| **Header (large) → Search** | **none** (`0`) | 0px | Header chrome supplies spacing; do not add margin/gap |
| **Header (large) → Tabs** | **`unit-2`** | 4px | Hairline step only |
| **Header (large) → first section cluster** | **`gap.xl`** | 8px | Tight step after the hero header to the first section block |
| **Header (`size="medium"` / small) → first scroll block** | **`gap.3xl`** | 16px | Put **`padding-top: $padding-vertical-3xl`** on the scroll/page column (or first block wrapper) so content clears header chrome consistently. |
| **Header (`size="medium"`) → first block when it is a marketing / hero headline** | **`gap.4xl`** | 24px | e.g. landing hero under title+subtitle — use a page modifier (e.g. **`pageFirstHero`**) instead of the default 16px step. |
| **SectionHeader → its Card / body** | **wrapper `gap: 0`** | 0px added | **Only** **`SectionHeader`’s** built-in **`padding-vertical-xl` (8px)** sits above the **`Card`**. **Do not** add **`gap.4xl`** between them. Wrap **`SectionHeader` + `Card`** in **`.sectionHeaderTight`** (or equivalent) if the page stack uses **`gap.4xl`** between other sections. |
| **Stacked `Card`s (listing / plan rows, same column)** | **`margin.horizontal-m`** | 12px | Vertical gap between stacked cards should **match the page gutter** for a uniform grid — use **`$margin-horizontal-m`**, not **`gap.4xl`**, unless the screen is explicitly “sparse sections.” |
| **Search → Tabs** (same cluster) | **`gap.3xl`** | 16px | Inside one Search + Tabs column |
| **Tabs → section body below** | **`gap.3xl`** | 16px | Tabs ship no bottom margin |
| **Between sections** (separate ideas: Card group → Card group) | **`gap.4xl`** | 24px | Default inter-section rhythm (use `gap.5xl` only when spec says so). **Exception:** **dense stacked cards** in one list — use **`margin.horizontal-m`** (12px); see row **Stacked `Card`s** above. |
| **Inside Card** (TextField → Chips, TextField → TextField, etc.) | **`gap.3xl`** | 16px | One flex column per card body stack. **Default:** primary **form fields** live **inside** a **`Card`** (or one card per logical group), not naked on the page wash unless the spec is edge-to-edge. |
| **`List` inside `Card`** (benefits, settings, payment rows) | **consumer `List` `customClass`** | — | Avoid **double horizontal inset**: apply **negative horizontal `margin`** on the **`List` ul root** equal to **`Card`’s horizontal `padding`**, with **`width: calc(100% + 2×padding)`**, so **`ListItem`’s** horizontal padding is the **only** inset. **Do not** override **`ListItem`** internals. |
| **Inside a text/copy cluster** (title → supporting line, label → helper) | **`gap.m`** – **`gap.xl`** | 4–8px | Proximity: lines that form one thought stay close |
| **Between separate clusters** (in sheets, disclaimers, etc.) | **`gap.2xl`** – **`gap.3xl`** | 12–16px | Separate ideas, still within one surface |
| **Chip → Chip** (horizontal row) | **`gap.xl`** | 8px | Not `gap.2xl` |
| **Quick-action icons** (horizontal row) | **`gap.3xl`** | 16px | Circular hit targets at `unit-13` (56px) |

**Common mistakes:** (1) Applying **`gap.4xl`** between **`SectionHeader`** and its **`Card`** — use a **`gap: 0`** wrapper (**`sectionHeaderTight`**) instead. (2) **`Alerts` `layout="inline"`** next to full-width **`Card`**s — the shipped **`width: calc(100% - 24px)`** + **`margin: 0 12px`** narrows the bar; pass **`customClass`** on **`Alerts`** with **`width: 100%`**, **`max-width: 100%`**, **`margin-inline: 0`** (**`!important`** if needed) so the alert matches the **content column**; keep **inner** padding on the alert root for copy/icon inset. (3) **Sum insured / discrete amounts** — prefer **`List`** + **`leading: radio`** (or **`Slider`** when continuous) over ad-hoc **`Button`** grids unless the pattern is explicitly CTA-style chips. (4) **`Alerts`** without **`LeadingIcon`** — copy hugging the left edge reads wrong; pass **`LeadingIcon`** (**`info`** for **`primary`**, **`pending_themed`** / notice-tinted for **`notice`**, **`success_themed`** for **`positive`**, **`failed`** family for **`negative`**) or add equivalent left inset in the library; see **PODS Components/Alerts** stories.

### 8.2 Layout ownership model

When adding or evaluating a component, classify it before changing spacing:

| Question | Typical answers |
|----------|-----------------|
| Who owns **outer horizontal inset** here? | page shell / **Card** / **BottomSheet** / full-bleed banner / row wrapper |
| Who owns **interior padding**? | the component root if it paints a surface or field shell |
| Who owns **vertical rhythm**? | page section stack / card content stack / sheet body stack / row internals |
| Who owns **separators / hairlines**? | the repeated row stack, stretched to the current inset owner |
| Who owns **portal attachment / clipping**? | root app for full-bleed layouts, or preview shell / local frame for framed layouts |

### 8.3 Component context guide

Use this as a default classification when extending rules to additional components:

| Component kind | Examples | Default treatment |
|----------------|----------|-------------------|
| **Page chrome** | **Header**, sticky top bars, bottom docks | Align to shell/page inset. May break out full width only when the pattern is explicitly edge-to-edge. |
| **Section labels** | **SectionHeader**, helper headings | Outside **Card** by default. **Horizontal:** when the page shell already applies **`margin.horizontal-m`**, cancel **`SectionHeader`’s horizontal root padding** via **`customClass`** (**`padding-left/right: 0`**) so the title aligns with the **Card** outer edge in the content column — do not stack **`padding-horizontal-3xl`** on **`SectionHeader`** with the page gutter. **Vertical:** no extra spacer before the following **`Card`** beyond **`SectionHeader`’s** own **`padding-vertical-xl`** (see §8.1a). |
| **Raised content surfaces** | **Card**, inline **Alerts**, grouped content blocks | Surface owns interior padding; children should not re-apply the same gutter. |
| **Field/control shells** | **Search**, **TextField**, **Dropdown**, **OTP**, **SegmentedControl** | Keep field-internal padding; add block spacing from the parent stack, not from arbitrary per-control margins. |
| **Repeating rows** | **ListItem**, settings rows, radio/checkbox rows, switch rows | Parent surface usually owns horizontal inset; rows may need padding reset and separator restretch. |
| **Meters / progress tracks** | **ProgressBar** (`data-testid="progress-bar-container"`) | **Fill the parent content width** (`width: 100%`, `box-sizing: border-box`, **no** horizontal **`margin`** on the component root). The **Card**, sheet body, or shell column already owns horizontal inset — extra margin on the bar **shortens** the track and reads as a second inset. Space from labels above/below comes from the **parent** stack **`gap.*`**, not from the bar’s side margins. |
| **Viewport-edge banners / docks** | block **Alerts**, docked **BottomNavBar**, floating CTA bands, sticky promo bands | Use breakout deliberately so the background reaches the device edge while interior copy/actions stay token-inset. |
| **Portaled overlays** | **BottomSheet**, **ActionSheet** (uses **BottomSheet**), popovers, menus | **`attachToElementID`** must target a **portal host inside `mobile-preview-shell`** for device-framed UIs — see §9 **Rule — BottomSheet and ActionSheet in a device frame**. Match clipping to the shell that launched them. |

