## 9. Responsive behaviour

This package is **component-level**; breakpoints are not centralised in `design-tokens.json` like a marketing site. Treat responsiveness as:

- **Per-component** behaviour documented in each story (fullscreen layout in `preview.js` encourages true mobile framing).
- **Consumer-owned** page grids — use the **number system** for consistent gutters and touch targets when implementing screens.

**Design-review / demo framing (consumer apps):** Full-screen flows (e.g. R&U prototypes at **376×812**, iPhone 13 Mini) use **two** wrappers so the flow is visually inside a **mobile preview frame** on desktop, not only a loose full-width column:

| Layer | Role | Typical class |
|--------|------|----------------|
| **Frame** | Outermost viewport wrapper: centers the preview, optional desk background (**`--surface-level-1`** or a neutral from `color-semantics` so it contrasts the flow background), safe-area / vertical padding so the preview does not hug the browser chrome. On real phones this layer is a **pass-through** (no extra inset). | e.g. **`mobile-preview-frame`** |
| **Shell** | **Direct parent of the flow root** (e.g. **`DthRechargeFlow`**): owns the **376×812** (or full-bleed) geometry, page wash, horizontal inset, and bottom padding. Use **`overflow: hidden`** on the shell and put **vertical scroll** only on an inner **`.mobile-preview-shell-scroll`** (flex **`flex: 1`**, **`min-height: 0`**, **`overflow-y: auto`**) so **`position: fixed`** **BottomSheet** overlays (portaled beside the scroll column) **do not** move when the user scrolls — if the portal lived **inside** the scrolling subtree, fixed sheets would **scroll away** with content and could create **phantom scroll** past the real page. Apply **horizontal page inset once** on the shell using **`number-semantics.margin.horizontal-m`**. See §11. | e.g. **`mobile-preview-shell`** |

**Behaviour**

- **Narrow viewport** (`max-width: 599px`): **frame** is neutral (block layout, no horizontal centering). **Shell** is **100% width**, **`min-height: 100vh`** — matches a physical device.
- **Wide viewport** (`min-width: 600px`): **frame** uses flex (or grid) to **horizontally center** the shell and optional vertical padding. **Shell** is **376px** wide, **height `min(812px, 100vh)`**, **`overflow: hidden`** — scroll the **`.mobile-preview-shell-scroll`** child when content exceeds the viewport. Optional: **`border-radius`** on the shell only, tied to **`number-semantics.radius.3xl`** (preview chrome), not a substitute for in-flow **Card** radius rules in §11.

**DOM expectation:** `div.mobile-preview-frame` → `div.mobile-preview-shell` → **`div.mobile-preview-shell-scroll`** → *(optional scroll-height stabiliser when bottom chrome must dock to the viewport edge)* content wrapper → **`Header`**, sections, **Card**s, **and** a **sibling** portal host on the **shell** (**`position: absolute`**, **`inset: 0`**, **`pointer-events: none`**) → **BottomSheet** roots (portaled into the host). Do not attach **`mobile-preview-shell`** only to `#root` without a **frame** when the spec calls for a centered device preview on desktop.

**Scroll viewport height & bottom-docked primary CTA:** Make **`.mobile-preview-shell-scroll`** a **flex column** with a definite height chain so short pages can still dock bottom chrome to the viewport edge. If the page has screen-level actions or a **BottomNavBar**, wrap body content in a growable column and keep the dock as a trailing sticky region. **Semantic placement:** actions that apply to the **whole screen** belong in the bottom dock; actions scoped to **one section** belong inside that section’s **Card**.

**Overlays inside the device shell (BottomSheet / portaled UI):** **PODS Components/BottomSheet** renders with **`createPortal`** and a **`position: fixed`** full-viewport container (`data-testid="bottom-sheet-container"`). The default **`attachToElementID`** is **`root`**, so the scrim and sheet **span the browser window**, not the **376px** preview — wrong for design-review shells.

**Rule — BottomSheet and ActionSheet in a device frame:** **`ActionSheet`** is built on **`BottomSheet`**. Whenever the flow sits inside **`mobile-preview-shell`** (Storybook preview or any centered **376px** shell), **`attachToElementID`** **must** target a **portal host `div` that is a direct child of that shell** (`position: absolute; inset: 0; z-index` above content; **`pointer-events: none`** on the host; sheet roots set **`pointer-events: auto`** when active) — **never** **`#storybook-root`**, **`#root`**, or **`document.body`**. Otherwise the scrim and sheet cover the **whole browser window** instead of staying **inside the device frame**. Use a fixed **`id`** (e.g. **`pods-sheet-portal`**) or React **`useId()`** for the host. Full-bleed apps with no preview shell may keep the default **`root`** attach target.

For flows inside **`mobile-preview-shell`**:

1. Wrap **scrollable** page content (**`Header`**, sections, **Card**s) in **`.mobile-preview-shell-scroll`**; keep **`overflow-y: auto`** on **that** wrapper only, not on the shell (shell **`overflow: hidden`** + flex column).
2. Mount the empty portal host as a **direct child** of the shell **after** **`.mobile-preview-shell-scroll`**, with **`position: absolute; inset: 0; z-index`** above the scroll layer and **`pointer-events: none`** (sheets set **`pointer-events: auto`** when active). **Sticky bottom dock:** On **`.mobile-preview-shell-scroll`**, prefer **`overflow-x: clip`** (not **`hidden`**) alongside **`overflow-y: auto`** so **`position: sticky; bottom: 0`** primary CTA / bottom chrome reliably sticks inside the scrollport in WebKit and Chromium. If the **shell height is not bounded** (page scroll outside the scroll column) or you need the CTA glued to the **device frame** regardless, use **`position: fixed`** bottom chrome (**`shellFixedBottomChromeStack`**) with an **in-flow** **`shellScrollInFlowBottomReserveForFixedChrome`** block last inside **`shellScrollMainGrow`** (reserve = chrome height + **`number-semantics.gap.4xl`** per §11 **Between sections**; do not rely on **`padding-bottom`** on the outer column — flex overflow can skip it), and keep the shell under **`transform`** so **`fixed`** is clipped to the frame. **Do not** shrink the preview shell below the §9 desktop geometry (**`376px` × `min(812px, 100vh)`**) with extra **`max-height: 100%`** on the shell — that breaks the defined device frame.
3. Pass **`attachToElementID`** to that host’s **`id`** on every **`BottomSheet`** and **`ActionSheet`** in that flow (same **`attachToElementID`** string as the host **`div`**).
4. On **`.mobile-preview-shell`**, set a non-**`none`** **`transform`** (e.g. **`translateZ(0)`**) so **`position: fixed`** **BottomSheet** containers use the **shell** as their **containing block**. **`position: relative`** on the shell for the absolute portal host.

Then **`--overlay-strong`** and the sheet panel are clipped to the **device frame** on desktop. Apps that are truly full-bleed (no preview shell) keep the default **`attachToElementID`** (**`root`**).

**Design-review note:** In a harness that compares right vs wrong behaviour, the **correct** reference should always attach the sheet to the shell portal host in framed layouts—never rely on **`document.body`** when a device frame is present.

**Single horizontal inset owner (shell vs component roots):** When **`mobile-preview-shell`** (or the app scroll column) applies the **12px** page gutter (**`margin.horizontal-m`** / **`unit-5`**), **do not** let PODS component **root** wrappers add **another** horizontal inset — typography and **Card** edges will misalign (e.g. **SectionHeader** uses **`padding-horizontal-3xl`** on **`section-header-container`**; **Header** uses **`padding-horizontal-2xl`** on its roots). **Consumer pattern:** under **`div.mobile-preview-shell`**, set **`padding-left`** and **`padding-right`** to **`0`** (**`!important`** if needed to beat CSS modules) on the component roots in the table below — **vertical** padding on those nodes stays as shipped.

**Exceptions — keep horizontal padding on these roots:** **Do not** zero these roots when applying the §9 strip. Their horizontal padding is **interior** inset (inside the control or raised surface within the shell’s content column), **not** a second **page** gutter. **Search** uses **`padding-horizontal-2xl`** for the field interior; stripping it removes icon/input inset. **Alerts** keeps **inner** horizontal padding on **`alerts-container`** for both **`layout="inline"`** and **`layout="block"`**; stripping it removes copy/icon inset inside the notice. **`layout="block"`** is for **viewport-edge** banners (e.g. sticky below the header or above the nav): span the **full shell width** with **negative horizontal margin** equal to the shell gutter so the **background** is flush to the device edge while **padding on the alert root** still insets the text. **`layout="inline"`** is for **in-flow** notices (section body, inside **Card**): rounded surface aligned to the **content column**; when the shell already applies **`margin.horizontal-m`**, cancel any component-level outer margin so inset is **not doubled**. The **`Alerts`** **`inline`** implementation also ships **`width: calc(100% - 24px)`** and **`margin: 0 12px`** — under a shell-owned gutter that **narrows** the notice vs sibling **Card**s. **Consumer rule:** when **`inline`** **Alerts** sit in the **same stacked column** as **Card**s (same content width as §11 **376px** column / **`~352px`** body), wrap them (or target **`alerts-container`**) so the root is **`width: 100%`**, **`max-width: 100%`**, **`margin-inline: 0`** (**`!important`** if needed to beat **`.inline`**), while **keeping** inner horizontal padding on the alert root for copy/icon inset. **Card** uses **`padding-horizontal-3xl` / `vertical-3xl`** for inner content inset. **SegmentedControl** uses **`padding-horizontal-s`** on the root container for track interior, not page gutter.

| `data-testid` | Component / notes |
|--------|-------------------|
| **`card`** | **Card** — inner content inset (**§11**, **`padding-horizontal-3xl` / `vertical-3xl`**) is not a duplicate page gutter. |
| **`search-container`** | **Search** — horizontal padding is **inside** the field shell (icon and input), not an extra page gutter. |
| **`alerts-container`** | **Alerts** — inner horizontal padding on the root for **inline** and **block** (do not strip); **`layout="inline"`** for in-flow / **Card**, **`layout="block"`** for sticky full-bleed banners (break out with negative horizontal margin so the background reaches the device edge while text stays inset). In a guttered column next to **Card**s, cancel **`inline`**’s outer width/margins so the bar matches the **content column** (see §9 prose above). |
| **`segmented-container`** | **SegmentedControl** — horizontal padding on the root is **track interior** (**`padding-horizontal-s`**), not a duplicate **page** gutter; stripping it flattens the control against the pill edge. |

| `data-testid` (root to zero horizontally under shell) | Component / notes |
|--------|-------------------|
| **`header-default`** | **HeaderDefault** (large / compound layouts) |
| **`header-regular-avatar`** | **HeaderDefault** medium, **HeaderRegularAvatar** |
| **`header-small-avatar`** | **HeaderSmallAvatar** |
| **`header-logo`** | **HeaderLogo** |
| **`header-search`** | **HeaderSearch** |
| **`section-header-container`** | **SectionHeader** |
| **`tabs-container`** | **Tabs** |
| **`dropdown`** | **Dropdown** |
| **`otp-container`** | **OTP** |
| **`passcode-container`** | **Passcode** |
| **`slider-container`** | **Slider** |
| **`activity-timeline-container`** | **ActivityTimeline** |
| **`bottom-nav-bar-container`** | **BottomNavBar** — §9 strip removes duplicate **root** horizontal padding only; the bar still lives inside the shell content column, so without a consumer breakout it stays inset by the shell gutter. When the nav sits inside the scrolling shell, use **`position: sticky; bottom: 0`** plus negative horizontal margin equal to the shell gutter and matching width so the bar is flush to the device edge and docks to the bottom of the scroll viewport. **When a primary CTA row sits directly above the nav:** wrap the CTA and **BottomNavBar** in a single sticky breakout region instead of docking the nav alone. Omit the breakout when the shell scroll column has no horizontal padding. |
| **`text-field-container`** | **TextField** (page or sheet: sheet panel / **Card** still owns outer inset) |
| **`grid-*-container`** | **Grid** — match **`[data-testid^="grid-"][data-testid$="-container"]`** |

**Extension rule:** Apply the same logic to similar components even if they are not named above. If a root wrapper adds page-like horizontal padding, strip it under a shell-owned gutter. If a root wrapper paints a field or surface, keep its interior padding and only cancel any extra outer margins. If a component can render both **in-flow** and **viewport-edge** variants, map those to **inline surface** vs **full-bleed breakout** semantics rather than treating them as unrelated layouts.

**Consumer strip completeness + no “second gutter” on body wrappers:** Screen-level CSS that zeroes horizontal padding on PODS roots next to a shell-owned gutter (e.g. **`rootPaddingReset`** beside **`scrollGutter`** / **`mobile-preview-shell`**) must target **every** strip-table **`data-testid`** that appears **anywhere** in that scroll column for that screen — including **`header-search`** when **Header Search** is used, and **all** **Header Default** layout roots: **`header-default`** (**`size="large"`**), **`header-regular-avatar`** (**`size="medium"`**), **`header-small-avatar`** (**`size="small"`**). Stripping only **`header-default`** leaves **double inset** on medium/small headers. **Missing** an entry **re-applies** a second horizontal inset on that row. **Body regions** nested inside an already-guttered scroll column (search results, lists, form columns) must **not** add another **`margin.horizontal-m`** / page-gutter padding on their **outer** wrapper; use **vertical** padding / **`gap.4xl`** between section clusters only (see **§11**).

**Sheets and cards:** **BottomSheet** **`bottomSheetContent`** is the horizontal inset owner for the sheet; still zero **TextField** / **SectionHeader** / **Tabs** / etc. under the shell when those nodes appear **inside** the sheet so their root padding does **not** add to the sheet’s padding. **List** / **ListItem** horizontal rules remain per §11 (e.g. strip **ListItem** row padding under sheet when the sheet owns inset). **Chips** use a **dynamic** `data-testid` (`type` prop) — use **`customClass`** or a scoped wrapper to avoid double inset until a stable test id exists.

