## 11. Screen layout composition — card sections (updated 6 Apr 2026)

Paytm-style product screens are usually built from **page chrome + stacked sections**. Anchor implementation to **PODS Components** in Storybook and **`number-semantics`** / **`color-semantics`** in `design-tokens.json` (surfacing as CSS variables from `variables.css`).

| Rule | Token / component reference |
|------|-----------------------------|
| **Page top** | Start with **PODS Components/Header/Header Default** (not **SectionHeader**). Use **`HeaderWrapper`** + status-bar reservation as in the Header stories. |
| **Header density by step** | **First screen of a flow (landing / entry):** **`HeaderDefault`** with **`size="large"`** — tall layout, `data-testid="header-default"`. The primary page title on the **second row** uses **`typography.scale.display3`** + **`typography.weight.bold`** + **`var(--text-neutral-strong)`** (Gen AI Header reference: Figma file `e58GKvGTgkVs6jputDoINS`, node **`118:4466`**). **Do not** repeat that same title in a following **SectionHeader** — **SectionHeader** labels *sections below* the hero, not the screen H1. **Later steps in the same flow:** **`size="medium"`** — compact single-row title chrome, `data-testid="header-regular-avatar"` (layout class `headerRegularAvatarContainer` in CSS modules). Use **`size="small"`** only when you need the denser variant from the **Header Default** story. **Long scroll columns with sticky top chrome:** **`position: sticky`**, **`top: 0`**, **inside** the shell content column (**retain** the shell gutter and component horizontal padding — **not** the same full-bleed breakout as docked bottom **BottomNavBar** unless the spec calls for edge-to-edge header). Prefer **surface** that matches the page wash (e.g. **`--surface-level-4`** on a level-4 wash); **no** bottom hairline on the sticky header unless the pattern specifies one. When product asks for **large → medium** on scroll, crossfade or transition so **`large`** eases into **`medium`**. |
| **Section titles** | **PODS Components/SectionHeader** marks a content group. Keep it **outside** **Card** so the label is not on the elevated surface. Put **Card** (or the section body) **next** in the tree with **no** **`margin-top`** between — see **Section header → Card** row below. **Default `size`:** **`extra-large`** — matches **`SectionHeader`**’s component default (**`title1-bold`**). Omit **`size`** in code unless you need a different density: use **`large`** or **`medium`** for a step down, **`small`** for dense secondary groupings. On typings that still require **`size`**, pass **`size="extra-large"`** for the default. **Dropdown** bottom-sheet header falls back to **`medium`** when **`bottomSheetHeaderProps.size`** is omitted (sheet chrome, not page **SectionHeader**). |
| **Page horizontal inset (376px artboard)** | Left and right inset on the flow root (**`mobile-preview-shell`** or equivalent scroll column) comes from **`number-semantics.margin.horizontal-m`** (**`number-primitives.unit-5`**). On the **376px** preview shell, this yields a **352px** content column. Apply **only here**, not again on an inner wrapper. |
| **Shell vs component horizontal padding** | If the shell owns the outer gutter, **remove horizontal padding** on PODS **roots** listed in **§9** (strip table). **Do not** strip roots in the **§9 exceptions** table: **`card`**, **`search-container`**, **`alerts-container`**, **`segmented-container`** — their horizontal padding is **interior** inset inside the surface/control, not a second page gutter (see **§9**). **Alerts:** map **`layout="inline"`** / **`layout="block"`** to **in-flow vs sticky banner**; cancel **inline**’s outer margins when the shell already gutters. |
| **SectionHeader — no side padding when outside Card** | The library wraps **SectionHeader** in **`padding-horizontal-3xl`**. With **§9** shell gutter, **zero horizontal padding** on **`section-header-container`** under **`mobile-preview-shell`** (see §9 table) so the title row aligns with **Card** edges. Do **not** add a **second** padded wrapper only for the header. |
| **SectionHeader — side padding when nested** | When **SectionHeader** is placed **inside** a **Card** or another container that already insets its children, **then** add horizontal inset (or rely on that parent) so the title aligns with inner content. |
| **Section header → Card — no extra margin** | When **SectionHeader** is **immediately** followed by **Card** (or the section’s main body block), **do not** add **`margin-top`** on **Card**, a spacer **`div`**, or a flex **`gap`** between header and card. Vertical space comes **only** from **SectionHeader**’s root **`padding-vertical-xl`** (**`number-semantics.padding.vertical-xl`**). Extra **`margin-top`** or **`gap.3xl` / `gap.4xl`** here **stacks** on that padding and over-separates the title from the card. If product needs a larger step, adjust **SectionHeader** tokens or variants in the library — not ad-hoc screen margins. |
| **Section header → Card — Fragment / flex pitfall** | **`<>...</>`** (**React Fragment**) does **not** produce a DOM node. If **SectionHeader** and **Card** are adjacent in JSX but the **DOM parent** is **`display: flex; flex-direction: column`** with a non-zero **`gap`** (e.g. **`gap.4xl`** between “sections”), flex sees **two** items (header, card) and applies **`gap` between them** — the same bug as an explicit spacer. **Pattern:** wrap **SectionHeader + its Card / body** in one real wrapper (**`div`** / **`section`** / styled block) with **`flex-direction: column`** and **`gap: 0`** (or plain block flow); use **`gap.4xl`** (or **`gap.5xl`**) **only between** those wrappers when separating major blocks. |
| **Section body on wash — stacked action rows** | When **SectionHeader** is followed by **two or more** sibling blocks **on the page wash** (**not** inside **Card**) — e.g. a **wrap** row of **Button**s, then a **full-width** **Button** below — **Button** does **not** add **margin-block** for the next sibling; without a wrapper the rows read as **vertically glued**. Wrap those **body** siblings (**only** the content **after** the header) in one **`flex`** column with **`number-semantics.gap.3xl`** (SCSS **`$gap-3xl`**) between **direct** children. **Do not** put **`gap.3xl`** between **SectionHeader** and the **first** body row — spacing from the title to the first block still comes **only** from **SectionHeader**’s **`padding-vertical-xl`** (see **Section header → Card — no extra margin**). **Example:** a **Documents**-style section on the wash — tonal **Button** row + **stroke** **Add e-card**. Same idea as **Card — vertical gap between stacked body blocks**, but for **wash-level** sections without a **Card** shell. |
| **Search → Tabs under shell gutter** | **Search** keeps **`padding-horizontal-2xl`** on **`search-container`** (field interior only). After the §9 strip, **`tabs-container`** must stay **0** horizontal on the root so **tab labels** align with **SectionHeader** titles and other **section body** type (**do not** re-add **`padding-horizontal-2xl`** on **`tabs-container`** — that would double inset the copy). Put **Search** and **Tabs** in one **`flex`** column and separate them with **`number-semantics.gap.3xl`**. When **Tabs** sit **immediately under** **Header** (no **SectionHeader** / body block between), use **`number-primitives.unit-2`** **`margin-top`** on **Tabs** instead of the larger section gap. |
| **Tabs → section body below** | **Tabs** do **not** ship **`margin-bottom`** on **`tabs-container`** for the **next** block (**Alerts**, **Card**, primary section content, etc.). After **SectionHeader** (or **Search** + **Tabs** cluster), add **`number-semantics.gap.3xl`** between **Tabs** and that following body. |
| **SegmentedControl inside Card — vertical order** | **`SegmentedControl`** must be the **first** block inside **Card**, or **second** when **SectionHeader** is the **first** child **inside** that **Card** (page-level **SectionHeader** for the section stays **outside** the card per **Section titles** row). Do **not** place **SegmentedControl** after **List** / **TextField** / **Chips** / other mid-card body — use another **Card** if you need that pattern. When **SegmentedControl** pairs with **`TextField`** at the **top** of the same card, order **segment** then **field** and separate with **`number-semantics.gap.3xl`**. **`§9`** root strips are **horizontal** only — use a **section-local** vertical **`gap`** inside the card for that step. **Top inset when first:** if the **Card** uses the compact top/bottom variant intended for padded row stacks, but **SegmentedControl** is the **first** child, restore the top inset to **`number-semantics.gap.2xl`** so the control does not sit too tight to the card edge. |
| **Header (large) cluster → first section block** | After **`HeaderDefault`** **`size="large"`** (back row + title block + any immediate header children), separate the **next** section’s chrome/body with **`number-semantics.gap.xl`** (`number-primitives.unit-4`, SCSS **`$gap-xl`**) — **except** when the **immediate** next block is **`Search`** (see **Search immediately under Header (large)**): **do not** insert extra vertical gap between **Header** and **`Search`**. |
| **Search immediately under Header (large)** | When **`Search`** is the **first** control **directly after** **`HeaderDefault`** **`size="large"`** (no **SectionHeader** or other body block between **`HeaderWrapper`** and **`search-container`**), **do not** add **`margin-top`**, **`padding-top`**, or flex **`gap`** between **Header** and **Search** (**`0`** extra — header chrome / title block supplies spacing above the field). **`gap.xl`** still applies **before the first true section cluster** **after** this **Search** (e.g. **SectionHeader** + **Card**) when the pattern calls for that step; it **does not** sit between **Header** and **Search**. **Similar density** to **Tabs** immediately under **Header** (**`unit-2`** **`margin-top`** on **Tabs** when that row needs a hairline step — **Search** defaults to **no** added margin). |
| **Between sections** | Separate stacked **section** blocks (after the first post-header block) with **`number-semantics.gap.4xl`** (`number-primitives.unit-8`) unless a product spec standardises on **`gap.5xl`**. |
| **Quick-action icon row** | Space adjacent circular actions with **`number-semantics.gap.3xl`**. Circular hit targets in that row use **`number-primitives.unit-13`** (56px; SCSS **`$unit-13`**) — do **not** invent intermediate sizes (e.g. 52px) when this spec applies. |
| **Primary content surface** | Put **List** / **ListItem** groups and grouped actions inside **PODS Components/Card** on a page wash such as **`--surface-level-4`**. Prefer the **Card** story defaults for fill. **Card inner padding** is **16px** on all sides — **`number-semantics.padding.horizontal-3xl` / `vertical-3xl`** (`number-primitives.unit-6`), applied in **`Card.module.scss`**. |
| **ProgressBar — full width of card / section body** | **PODS Components/ProgressBar** must **span the full inner width** of its parent (**`width: 100%`**, **`box-sizing: border-box`**) with **no** horizontal **`margin`** on **`progress-bar-container`** — the parent (**Card**, **BottomSheet** body, etc.) already applies content inset; margin on the bar **narrows** the track (**~32px** loss with **16px** sides) and misaligns with sibling copy. Use the **parent** vertical **`gap.*`** for space above/below the bar. **Storybook:** **PODS Components/ProgressBar**; full-page composition examples live in **`docs/layout-references/layouts.md`**. |
| **List row dividers — no line on last row** | In a stacked list (**List** / **ListItem**, manual rows in a **Card**, etc.), dividers belong **between** items only. The **final row** must **not** have a **bottom** rule (**`border-bottom`**, **ListItem `separator`** line, or equivalent). For **PODS ListItem**, set **`separator={false}`** on the last item (or **`separator={index < length - 1}`** when mapping). Use **`border-top`** / leading dividers on **2nd+** rows if building custom stacks. Divider colour: **`--border-neutral-weak`** (or **Separator** from Storybook where used). **Row height** is driven by content, line count, and tokenised padding — **do not** fix a pixel row height in prompts or specs. |
| **ListItem — leading Avatar raster** | **`leading.type="avatar"`** uses **`Avatar`** logo/profile rasters inside a fixed-diameter chip. **Do not** stretch those **`img`** nodes with consumer CSS; rely on **`Avatar.module.scss`** (**`object-fit: cover`**, etc.) per **§5.4**. |
| **Card padding** | **Intent:** the card shell should add **comfortable vertical inset** whenever the inner content does **not** already bring its own “row” padding at the top and bottom edges. Default **PODS Card** content inset is **`number-semantics.padding.horizontal-3xl`** and **`vertical-3xl`**. **When to tighten top/bottom (compact):** use the same horizontal inset but reduce the card’s **top/bottom** to **`number-primitives.unit-2`** **only** when the card is **mostly a stack of padded rows** — e.g. **ListItem** rows, in-card **SectionHeader**-style rows — so you do **not** double vertical padding with the row chrome. **Do not** treat “any card” as compact because a **List** appears elsewhere on the screen: **per-card** choice. **Non-row interiors** (plain typography, **Chips** + helper copy, promo blocks, mixed copy + controls without row wrappers) should keep **default vertical-3xl**; use a **section-local** **`gap`** (e.g. **`gap.3xl`**) between inner blocks for rhythm inside the padded shell. **Sub-exception — segment first in a compact list card:** **`SegmentedControl`** as the **first** child is **not** a heavy row; if the rest of the card is a compact list stack, restore **Card** **top** to **`number-semantics.gap.2xl`**. Do not rely on ad-hoc `px` in consumers unless **`customClass`** intentionally overrides. |
| **Card vertical compact — row stacks only** | The **compact** top/bottom ( **`unit-2`**) is for **list / row-stack** cards where **first and last** visible blocks are row components that already add vertical padding. **Do not** use it when the main body is **only** **TextField**(s), **Chips**, free-form copy, or other blocks **without** that row padding — the surface looks **pinched** and helpers sit too close to the rounded corners. **Do not** use it for “marketing” or **summary copy** cards even if they sit next to list cards on the same page. Reserve **compact** for **List**-heavy cards (and **§11** segment-first top exception when applicable). |
| **Card — do not shrink padding for multi-line + CTA tiles** | Do **not** set **`Card`** **`customClass`** padding to **`padding-vertical-m`** (**`number-semantics.padding.vertical-m`**, 4px) for cards whose interior is **several lines** (title, meta, status) **plus** a **Button** or other block actions — that **removes** visible card inset and content hugs the rounded corners. Keep **default** **`padding-vertical-3xl` / `padding-horizontal-3xl`** from **`Card.module.scss`** for **claim summaries**, **order / transaction detail** tiles, **notification**-style blocks, and similar. Reserve **`padding-vertical-m`** **only** for **true single-row** tiles that mirror **List** row density (e.g. **recent-spend** list row cards). **Claims**-style summary cards follow the **default** **Card** inset. |
| **TextField internal stack (PODS common)** | **PODS Components/TextField** sets **`colGap`** **`number-semantics.gap.m`** on **`data-testid="text-field-container"`** between the **input row** and **infoSection** (assistive / error). **Align screens with that default** — **do not** override **`gap`** on **`text-field-container`** in consumer CSS unless a **written product spec** asks for extra air (e.g. dense multi-line helper copy); ad-hoc **`gap.xl`** drifts from Storybook and the library. **Between** stacked fields in the same **Card**, spacing comes from the parent stack (**`number-semantics.gap.3xl`**, e.g. **`shellInsetCardBlockStack`**), not from widening the field’s own internal gap. Where flex layouts need it, keep **`width: 100%`** and **`min-width: 0`** on the field root so the control does not **shrink-wrap**. See **§13** for a short TextField / list-avatar reminder. |
| **Card corner radius** | Screen- and section-level **Card** surfaces on neutral washes use **`number-semantics.radius.3xl`**, backed by **`number-primitives.unit-8`** (24px in `design-tokens.json` / **PODS Number System** radius scale). **`data-testid="card"`** wrappers in product UIs should resolve to this radius (SCSS **`$radius-3xl`** or equivalent from `Number.mdx`). If the **PODS Components/Card** story ships a smaller radius, override via **`customClass`** or shared Card styling so production cards match **`radius.3xl`**. |
| **Card — borderless section tiles on wash** | **PODS Card** (**`pods-components/Card/Card.module.scss`**) defaults to **`border: 1px solid`** **`--border-neutral-weak`** on **`cardWrapper`** so surfaces read as **boxed** on ambiguous backgrounds. That default is **not** turned off by **`.storybook/`** preview config — product screens must override in **`customClass`** when the pattern calls for borderless tiles. On a **page wash** (e.g. **`--surface-level-4`**), **section** cards that should read as **soft tiles** (category grids, hub shortcuts, grouped content that already separates from the wash via **`surface-level-1`** fill + **`radius.3xl`**) should **not** keep that hairline — it **double-defines** the edge. **Consumer pattern:** set **`border: none`** (or **`0`**) on **`customClass`** for those cards, **keeping** token fill + radius. **Do** keep the default **Card** border when the pattern needs a **strong** control outline on the same plane as neighbours. |
| **Avoid double padding** | Do **not** combine **Card**’s own padding, a **manual padded `div`**, **and** components that already carry horizontal gutters (**List** / **ListItem** row padding, **TextField**, etc.). That stacks insets (e.g. card inset + **ListItem** **`padding-horizontal-3xl`** on **`data-testid^="list-item-"`**) and narrows content twice. **Inside Card, the Card owns horizontal inset:** suppress **ListItem** left/right padding so row text aligns to the card content box. Same pattern as sheets: when the parent owns inset, strip duplicate row gutters. **Pick one inset owner** if you override **Card** via **`customClass`** — confirm spacing in Storybook for each pair. **OTP inside Card:** **`otp-container`** applies vertical padding from tokenised padding values; when **Card** owns outer inset, remove the OTP root’s extra top/bottom padding so the control does not double the card’s vertical breathing room. |
| **List row hairlines — inset owner** | **PODS ListItem** draws the **Separator** in a wrapper sized for rows that still have **`padding-horizontal-3xl`**. If you strip row horizontal padding because **Card** (or sheet) owns inset, **re-stretch** the separator wrapper to the **same** horizontal span as the content surface: **inside Card**, hairlines must run to the **Card inner edge**. **On the page wash** (**List** **not** inside **Card**) with the §9 shell gutter, hairlines should extend to the intended screen edge if the pattern calls for full-width dividers. Do **not** leave a separator wrapper sized for the old inset after stripping row padding; the line will sit short of the correct edge. |
| **Chips — horizontal gap in a row** | When several **PODS Components/Chips** sit **in one row** (**`display: flex`**, **`flex-wrap`** as needed), space **between** chips is **`number-semantics.gap.xl`**. Do **not** reuse **`gap.2xl`** for chip-to-chip spacing — that step is for a different density on the number scale. |
| **Card — vertical gap between stacked body blocks** | **`TextField`** (and similar controls) do **not** add **block-level** space **below** the field for the **next** sibling. Internal **`colGap`** only separates the input row from assistive copy **inside** the component. When **`TextField`** is followed by **`Chips`**, **`Button`**, another **`TextField`**, or other mid-card blocks **inside** the **same** **Card**, put those siblings in one **section-local** **`flex`** column with **`number-semantics.gap.3xl`**. **Do not** assume the library field will **margin** itself away from the next control. |
| **Floating primary CTA above BottomNavBar** | On a **page wash** (for example **`--surface-level-4`**) with a shell-owned gutter, use **`Button`** **`type="filled"`** for the main row **above** a **BottomNavBar** when that pattern applies. Wrap the **CTA** and **BottomNavBar** in one **`position: sticky`**, **`bottom: 0`** column so both **dock** together — **CTA** **above** the tab bar. Inside that stack, the **CTA** sits in a full-width **surface-level-1** band with **`padding: number-semantics.gap.xl`** around the control; apply gutter breakout on the stack wrapper when the shell gutters so the plate + nav span the device edges. When there is **no** bottom nav, use only the CTA band + breakout — no empty nav slot wrapper. Pair this with the §9 scroll-height rule so short pages still fill the preview height and the bar sits flush to the bottom edge. |
| **BottomSheet width + inset** | **PODS Components/BottomSheet** applies **`padding`** on **`bottomSheetContent`** (`data-testid="bottom-sheet"`). Slotted children (`data-testid="children"`) should **span the full inner width** (**`width: 100%`**, **`align-self: stretch`**, **`min-width: 0`** on flex descendants) so lists and forms are not shrink-wrapped. Treat the **sheet panel as the horizontal inset owner** for that region: **do not** add a second horizontal padded wrapper around sheet children, and **suppress built-in row gutters** on **ListItem** (or equivalent) inside the sheet — otherwise text rows stay narrow and insets **double**. Override via scoped CSS (for example zero **`padding-left` / `padding-right`** on **`[data-testid^="list-item-"]`** under the sheet) or **`customClass`** on **List** / **ListItem** where the library supports it. After stripping row horizontal padding on **List** inside a sheet, re-stretch row blocks and **Separator** hairlines so they span the **sheet inner content width** (same §11 **List row hairlines — inset owner** rule as **Card**). **`children`** is a **flex** column with **`gap.3xl`** between **direct** children only; if you wrap several **`TextField`** or body blocks in one inner **`div`**, that outer gap does **not** space the wrapped controls. In that case use an inner **flex** column with **`gap.3xl`** plus matching top/bottom padding so the first and last controls get the same step from the sheet header and action row. **Spacing rule:** use **either** a single parent **`gap.3xl`**, **or** plain block flow with **`margin-block: gap.3xl`** on each control root so vertical margins collapse to one step between neighbours — **do not** put **`margin-block`** on every **`TextField`** **inside** a **flex** column that already has **`gap.3xl`**; **flex** **does not** collapse those margins, and **gap + margins** adds. |
| **BottomSheet — copy and info bodies (grouping)** | Sheets that are mostly **explanatory or legal copy** (not a spaced **form** stack) should still follow **§8.1 Proximity beats generic gaps**. Wrap each **logical cluster** (e.g. headline + supporting line, or disclaimer + text link) in a **single** inner column: use **`gap.m`**–**`gap.2xl`** **inside** a cluster — tighter between lines that are **one** thought (**`gap.m`** or **`gap.xl`** between title + supporting line is appropriate); use **`gap.2xl`**–**`gap.3xl`** **between** separate clusters only. **Do not** paste the same **form-body** wrapper used for **TextField** stacks (extra **`padding-top` / `padding-bottom`** on the consumer root) onto **copy-only** bodies — **BottomSheet** **`bottomSheetContent`** and **`contentSection`** already set vertical rhythm; **double padding** reads as **over-spaced**. **Component choice:** when the sheet chrome already carries a **title** + **description**, avoid piling **SectionHeader** **`extra-large`** in **`children`** (duplicate hierarchy + **SectionHeader** root **`padding-vertical-xl`**). Prefer a compact **`typography.scale`** stack (e.g. **`title3`** + **`body`**) or **`SectionHeader`** **`medium`** / **`large`** only if the pattern must stay component-pure. **Alignment:** copy clusters should be **left-aligned** (**`text-align: left`**, **`align-items: flex-start`** on the stack). **Inline copy actions** (**`Button`** **`type="link"`**): use **`medium`** (or another non-**large** size) so the control is **not** full-width; align to the **reading edge** (scoped **`padding-left`** reset when needed). If every short line is its **own** direct child of **`children`**, the component’s **`gap.3xl`** will **over-separate** — **group** in wrappers rather than “same gap everywhere.” |
| **Token-only inset (override Card default)** | **Card** defaults to **`padding.*.3xl`**. If a screen spec needs a different inset, override once via **`customClass`** (or a wrapper) — still avoid stacking with **List** / **ListItem** / **TextField** gutters. |

**Layout check (DOM / React):** preview frame (when used) → shell/root layout with the outer page inset and overlay containing block → **Header Default** (**`size="large"`** on landing: primary title is **`display3`** on the header’s second row — **not** duplicated in **SectionHeader**) → **Search** (when **immediate** next control: **no** extra margin vs header — **Search immediately under Header (large)**) → **`gap.xl`** before the **first** **SectionHeader** / section body cluster **after** that **Search** when the screen uses the large landing step → **SectionHeader** (**`size`** defaults to **`extra-large`**) → **Card** **directly** (**no** **`margin-top`** / spacer after **SectionHeader** — spacing from header **`padding-vertical-xl`** only) → inside **Card**: optional in-card **SectionHeader** first, else **`SegmentedControl`** (if any) **before** **List** / **TextField** / other body — never **SegmentedControl** mid-stack after list/fields unless it lives in a **separate** **Card** → wrap **List** + **TextField** + **Chips** + other stacked body blocks in a single vertical stack with **`number-semantics.gap.3xl`** so each block is separated from the next — **List** / **ListItem** (strip row horizontal padding inside **Card** when **Card** owns inset; **no** bottom divider on the last row) → **BottomSheet** (portal + full-width **`children`**, sheet-owned inset — no duplicate **ListItem** horizontal padding; for multi-field sheet bodies, use one inner vertical stack with matching top/bottom inset as described in **BottomSheet width + inset**; for **copy-heavy** sheet bodies, cluster related lines per **BottomSheet — copy and info bodies** and **§8.1 Proximity**). Further stacked **sections** use **`gap.4xl`** (or **`gap.5xl`** if the spec adopts it globally), never **`gap`** between **SectionHeader** and its **Card**.

