## 13. Consumer screen patterns (TextField, list avatars)

**Cross-reference:** extends **§8–§11** (composition, responsive shell, agent prompts, card sections).

### 13.1 TextField inside Card

- **Internal rhythm:** **`paytm_common_ui` TextField** uses **`number-semantics.gap.m`** (`colGap`) on **`[data-testid="text-field-container"]`** between the bordered **input** block and **assistive** / **error** copy. Treat that as the source of truth; match Storybook **PODS Components/TextField**.
- **Do not** override **`gap`** on **`text-field-container`** in consumer CSS unless product spec requires it.
- **Between fields:** parent stack **`gap.3xl`** (e.g. **`shellInsetCardBlockStack`**), not a wider internal field gap.
- **Flex safety:** **`width: 100%`** / **`min-width: 0`** on the field root in columns is fine when needed.

### 13.2 ListItem — leading avatar (people / beneficiaries)

Use **one consistent recipe** anywhere a row represents a **person or saved payee** (recent contacts, “Sending to”, “To”, beneficiary summary rows):

| Rule | Detail |
|------|--------|
| **Component** | **PODS Components/List** + **ListItem** with **`leading={{ type: "avatar", size: "regular", avatar: … }}`** — see **List** stories (*With leading avatar*, profile vs initials). |
| **Size** | **`size: "regular"`** on **`leading`** for standard product list density (step up from **`small`** only when spec demands). |
| **Photo** | **`avatar: { type: "profile", avatarProfile: { imageURL } }`** when the domain model has a URL (e.g. **`RecentContact.avatarUrl`**). |
| **No photo** | **`avatar: { type: "initials", avatarInitials: { initials } }`** — derive initials from **display name** (words → first letters; single token → up to two letters). Default **`initialsColor`** from the library is fine. |
| **Same beneficiary everywhere** | Checkout / success / sheets must show the **same** avatar logic as the contact list: **resolve** the row against **saved contacts** (match mobile/UPI), then fall back to initials from number/UPI local-part — do not hand-pick different **`Avatar`** styles per screen. |
| **Mixed lists (text-only rows + beneficiary)** | When some **`ListItem`** rows have **no** leading chrome and one row shows a person, put the avatar on **`trailing: { type: "avatar", avatar, size }`** so **primary/secondary** text stays left-aligned with other rows. **`leading.avatar`** stays the default for **all-avatar** lists (e.g. recent contacts). Library: **`paytm_common_ui` `ListItem`** trailing **`type: "avatar"`** (since **3.1.0** in this repo). |
| **Helpers** | Reuse one shared module for **`recentContactListLeading`** / **`recentContactTrailing`**, **`recipientListTrailing`** (and **`recipientListLeading`** when the whole list is avatar rows), with a single **`listLeadingAvatarSize`**. |
| **Not for every row** | Rows that are **fees**, **metadata**, **payment rails**, or **institution names** keep **icons**, **logos**, or **no** leading — avatars are for **identity**, not generic list chrome. |

When adding a new flow with payees, copy the **helper + types** pattern (`RecentContact` + optional **`avatarUrl`**) rather than inlining different **`Avatar`** props per file.

